 "ownerDecisions": [
  "Q-SOL-1 (lane monitor, owner-delegated, 2026-10-17, as HS53's amendment record holds it, verbatim): \"Q-SOL-1 (a): two packets, (1) the W01 amendment (OBSERVER row, I01 only) plus seccomp v5, and (2) programs v3 plus edge v5. The stale H:446-447 pointer gets fixed in packet 1.\"",
  "F-SOL-1's note (lane monitor, 2026-10-17, as HS53's amendment record holds it, verbatim): \"Note: \"edge v5\" for packet 2 will collide in name with native-profile v4's edge record v5 (slot 246). Check the next free edge version at drafting time; it is probably v6.\"",
  "Q-P2-1..4 (lane monitor, owner-delegated, consistent with 240's owner-approved PROGRAMS-REPUBLISH pattern, 2026-10-18, verbatim): \"SLOT 249 = MET-ENFORCE-036 is confirmed (not on main, unclaimed), branch codex/met-enforce-036-observer-programs-v3, and harness-onion-obsprog is registered as your worktree. Monitor decisions, consistent with 240's owner-approved PROGRAMS-REPUBLISH pattern (I'll tell the owner): Q-P2-1 (a): only OBSERVER's two programs plus the index of 14. Q-P2-3 (a): keep the seccomp-v3 OBSERVER rows for HE-004 unchanged. Q-P2-4 (a): one or two light contract-review rounds, then adoption, then mechanics on template 248, then the packet review. Q-P2-2: I've asked the primary for the HE-004-I01 vendor path(s), path level only, and will relay the answer. Until then, draft the rows as (a) with the seccomp-v5/ path. GO for the contract draft and the contract review rounds (light work). The pre-check, dry run and push need my word.\"",
  "Q-P2-2 (lane monitor, relaying the primary lane's facts at path level, 2026-10-18, verbatim): \"Q-P2-2 = (a), with the primary lane's facts at path level: HE-004-I01 vendors host-enforcement/contracts/seccomp-v5/OBSERVER.x86_64.bpf and host-enforcement/contracts/seccomp-v5/OBSERVER.aarch64.bpf, mode 100644, REGISTERED_BEFORE_USE. This follows R10's convention contracts/seccomp-v<N>/<ROLE>.<arch>.bpf, where N is the seccomp contract version compiled from. No other file is decided. R10 has never vendored allowlists or spec texts, so v5's allowlists and HS53's effective spec need no rows. A possible I01 wire vector comes in a later edge record. The v3 OBSERVER rows stay unchanged, per Q-P2-3 (a). Register the two .bpf rows only.\""
 ],
