  "Both new rows carry providerCommit null and providerPacket MET-ENFORCE-036, edge v3's convention for packet-published files: their commit is that packet's merge commit.",
  "Edge v2's two OBSERVER rows (HE-004, host-enforcement/contracts/seccomp-v3/) are carried unchanged (Q-P2-3 (a)). Whether R10 keeps contracts/seccomp-v3/OBSERVER.* is R10's decision; schema v2 has no status for a retired row, so a later record drops or retires those two rows if R10 removes the files.",
  "No other file is registered: R10 has never vendored allowlists or spec texts, so seccomp v5's allowlists and HS53's effective text need no rows, and a possible I01 wire vector comes in a later edge record (Q-P2-2 (a))."
